#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""T9 catalog: the red-team b1mech mechanical checks over EVERY entry of data/docs.curated.json
(FIXES #160, redteam 2026-10-09 F7). Rows tier,check,path,status,detail -> results/t9_catalog.csv, rewritten
whole each run (no resume: every entry is re-checked every time, same lesson as #32/#124).

  year      y is 4 digits 1500-2026 and appears in the document text or the filename; any (year) in t equals y
  lang      l is ISO 639-1; text stopword/script vote, and s/a votes, agree with l; VNI mojibake
  dose      t/s/a carry no dose figure (en+es DOSE pattern)
  echo      s/a are sentences, not prompt echoes / template fragments / mojibake / question lists
  audience  no survivalist wording outside the survival shelves
  empty     every entry has a one-line `s` and an answer `a` (RT3 #184: five r28 relabels lost `s` and this tier passed);
            #285: except a field listed in the entry's "c1" (C1 dropped its every sentence)
  c1        (#285, round 11 class 8) no s/a sentence carries a digit, the historical warning line excepted
  legal     firearms entries about making a machine gun / silencer / grenade launcher carry a legal line and no private-owner
            audience sentence (RT4 #195: two conversion manuals told owners to "attempt the conversion")
  front     s/a are not built from the publisher's ad pages: 3+ of their content words (40%+ of those the text holds) occur on
            ad pages and on at most one other page (RT5 #203: Rustic Carpentry described Hasluck's Handicraft Series ads)
  (audience, RT5 #205: the named-reader words "survivalists", "preppers", "Für Überlebende" are checked on every shelf;
            RT6 L5: "Survivors ... should open it" off the survival paths, and invented reading years "open it in 1914")
  copied    (RT6 L5, b1mech c5 gap) the core title (parentheticals and numbers out) equals the title of a file in ANOTHER folder
            whose file name shares no 4+ letter word: a title copied from another work (horology course titled as an NWTND
            chapter, TurboStove on the FEMA wood-gas manual, PCR Tool 5 on Tool 8, Where There Is No Dentist on HCWB ch. 8)
  slug      (RT6 L5, b1mech c7 gap) every title word comes from the file name and one of them is a catalogue code
            (Gtz100be, 100WWOOD), a 6+ letter all-caps non-word (PUBSBASN), a bare language code (En, Sp), or the title
            starts lower case ("fruit conserve (French)"): the file-stem slug with spaces that the old rule missed
  yearclaim (RT6 L5, b1mech c9 gap; the old grounding check gave 40 false positives and caught no swap) a year in s/a that is
            not y and not in t, the file name or the text: a summary copied from another work ("A guide from 1917 ..." on
            the Alcohol Fuels manual). Entries written from page images (src=vl) are skipped: their text layer is not what
            the model read
  fileyear  (RT6 L5, b1mech c1 gap) NOTE only, never FAIL: y appears in the file name only, not in a usable text layer whose
            first 10 pages print an imprint year (copyright, "entered ... in the year") that differs. Counted for the next
            audit round (most are probably later printings; each needs a page read)

Rules, regexes and the hand-checked false positives are imported from the red-team scripts
(b1mech_checks.py, b1mech_report.py beside this file, promoted from red-team round 20261009) so the tier and the audit agree.
Document text: gen_text's pdftotext cache (cache/pdftext); a miss runs pdftotext to memory.
Run with the sandbox disabled; log to logs/t9_catalog.log (progress every 1000 entries).
"""
